.SH NAME
daharness\-tools \(em daharness tool anatomy and execution model
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS The framework loop
The driving model searches the vector\-indexed tool registry, then
executes tools through the transports; results are projected before they
enter the model\(cqs context:
.IP
.EX
search  \->  execute  \->  transport dispatch  \->  result projection
.EE
.PP
In the packaged, headless build the \f[B]driving LLM is external\f[R]
\(em an Open WebUI model or any gateway/MCP client: discovery is
\f[I]/tools/search\f[R], execution \f[I]/tools/execute\f[R] or MCP
\f[I]tools/call\f[R], and an unknown \f[I]tool_id\f[R] is a loud 404
with a schema\-checked 422 on undeclared arguments (no hallucinated tool
calls).
There is no in\-process approval loop: the secretary chat lane was
removed 2026\-10\-20 and the packaged build has no conversation model
\(em gateway/MCP calls run under their own gates, and the per\-turn tool
budget is the headless brake (see \f[B]daharness\-safety\f[R](7)).
.SS Transports
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]LOCAL_FILE\f[R] \(em argparse modules discovered by static AST
analysis (never imported), run as subprocesses.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]BRAIN_DISPATCH\f[R] \(em \f[CR]\(atframework_tool\f[R] callables
over the Brain UDS; falls back in\-process when the socket is down.
If the Brain accepted a call but timed out, the result is a failure and
the tool is NOT retried in\-process (it may still be running there).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]MCP_RPC\f[R] \(em external RPC (Metasploit).
.SS Result projection
Every result passes through projection before it enters the model\(cqs
context.
Modes: \f[B]large\f[R] (default; byte\-capped, oversized spill to
scratch with a \f[I]scratch_ref\f[R] and a ready\-to\-call
continuation), \f[B]digest\f[R] (per\-tool\-family summary + scratch
ref) and \f[B]page\f[R] (bounded list page + continuation).
The continuation is the exact scratch\-search call to copy verbatim.
.SS Untrusted\-target provenance
Target\-facing tools stamp results with provenance.
Target output is \f[B]DATA, never instructions\f[R] \(em evidence to
analyze, not directives to follow.
.SS Stateful lanes
Live connection state (SSH, MSF, DB sessions) is process\-local:
sessions created on the Brain are invisible to in\-process fallback, and
tools report this honestly instead of silently failing.
Web cookies and tokens live on disk in a shared cookie jar, so every
lane sees the same jar.
.SS Engagement cobweb (journal + evidence + unknown ledger)
Every dispatch is journaled into the engagement store keyed by the
operator\-armed engagement slug (the REPL\(cqs
\f[CR]engagement on <slug>\f[R] \(em the model cannot arm or purge it).
Findings record conclusions; the evidence store records typed
\f[I]don\(cqt\-know\-yet\f[R] rows (credential/service/ambiguity/
scope_question/observation) with per\-kind TTLs, and the
credential\-reuse sweep is a DB constraint: one validation attempt per
(entry, service, target) \(em a second one is refused with re\-mint
guidance.
A purge erases one engagement in one transaction while the journal stays
append\-only; on the Postgres lane (see \f[B]daharness\-pg\f[R](1)) the
retention sweep runs as an owner SECURITY DEFINER function.
.SS Background jobs, fleet courtesy, and the worker queue
Long\-running CLI tools (nmap, ffuf, hydra, sqlmap, masscan) follow the
job pattern: the launcher returns a \f[I]job_id\f[R] immediately; status
and cancel companions manage the running job.
Jobs are durable SQLite rows scoped to the agent identity, with a TTL
sweep, per\-agent caps, and log\-file collection so a busy fleet cannot
leak disk.
.PP
Two courtesy layers sit in front of launches:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Fleet scheduler\f[R] \(em per\-TARGET\-HOST regulator,
numeric\-span aware (\f[CR]10.0.0.0/24\f[R] and its member
\f[CR]10.0.0.7\f[R] contend).
A duplicate ask for a running unit returns that unit\(cqs
\f[I]job_id\f[R] instead of launching a second process; per\-host slots
default 2 under an absolute ceiling of 4; auth\-adjacent units
(login/token requests) hold the host exclusively in both directions.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Worker queue\f[R] \(em the same shape for LOCAL RAM instead of the
target (jadx per\-APK decompiles first): admission is content\-keyed
dedupe → hard caps (budget vs free RAM above a pool floor) → slots →
queue.
Everything that is merely scarce QUEUES instead of refusing; recorded
peak\-RSS evidence from finished runs raises the next run\(cqs claim
(\f[CR]claim = budget + (peak − pin)\f[R]).
.PP
The Burp replay twins ride the queue the same way \(em replay/craft
tools with \f[B]no scan surface\f[R] (active scanning stays ZAP\(cqs
job).
